from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'stage/06f66ec88e8d/astraupskill'
common='The staged change maps Prisma error code P2025, which means the target row disappeared between the accessible pre-read and the transactional update, to the service AppError 404 contract. Unrelated errors are rethrown unchanged. The runtime check executes the actual TypeScript service with explicit repository, permission, Prisma transaction, and error doubles; it does not open a database or run Next.'
replace={
'README.md':'This lesson follows an administrative route-status update through permission checks, a scoped pre-read, lifecycle validation and persistence. The correction handles a missing update target consistently with the existing not-found contract. A P2025 failure from the transaction is mapped to AppError 404; unrelated failures remain operational errors. Concurrent deletion is one motivating scenario, not a forensic fact established by the error code or the test.',
'01-CODEBASE-MAP.md':'Follow the error toward its consumer as well as toward its source. The service uses the actual AppError class from src/lib/errors.ts; the admin route invokes transitionRouteStatus after request validation. The repository update is inside the transaction callback, while the accessible read and lifecycle checks occur before it. This placement explains both the missing-row error case and the remaining gap between checking a status and writing it.',
'02-CONCEPTS.md':'Provider error codes describe storage failures; domain errors describe the service contract presented to callers. Translation should be local to a boundary whose operation gives the code meaning. Here, the transaction contains one route update. If future code adds unrelated writes to the same transaction, a broad transaction-level P2025 catch could mislabel another missing record as a missing route. That future change should revisit the classification boundary.',
'04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md':'The expanded suite loads the actual transition service, AppError class and role-capability policy. Repository calls and the Prisma transaction are explicit adapters. Five named cases cover P2025 translation, unrelated object and primitive errors, successful return identity and transaction-handle wiring, analyst refusal, and a matrix of missing route, illegal transition and absent activation policy. This checks preconditions as well as the new error branch without pretending to execute Prisma.',
'VERIFICATION.md':'The accepted focused suite executes production transition logic, the real role policy and the real AppError. It supplies only repository and transaction boundaries relevant to this operation. Five cases cover mapped missing-target failure, unrelated failures, normal success, permission refusal and pre-write validation failures. The former two-case agent check is preserved as historical evidence, while the expanded root run is the accepted result.'
}
for f in p.glob('*.md'):
 s=f.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig').replace(common,replace.get(f.name,common))
 s=s.replace('P2025 is a storage boundary signal for that race.','P2025 indicates a required record was not found by the operation; concurrent deletion is a possible cause in this update path.')
 s=s.replace('The staged test covers a concurrent deletion and a sentinel database outage.','The test simulates a missing-row error after a successful pre-read and a sentinel persistence failure.')
 s=s.replace('The original service and test are preserved','The original service is preserved')
 s=s.replace('The original service and existing test are snapshotted.','The original service is snapshotted; the native test file is unchanged.')
 s=s.replace('the two runtime assertions','the five runtime cases').replace('Result: 2/2 passed. Cases are P2025 to 404 and unrelated persistence error identity preservation.','Result: 5/5 passed in the accepted expanded suite; see the captured evidence below.')
 s=s.replace('The two tests intentionally use different failure objects so classification and identity preservation are both visible.','The error case includes an Error, an unrelated code object, null and a string so the guard cannot accidentally assume every thrown value is a conventional Error.')
 s=s.replace('permission, Prisma transaction, and error doubles','Prisma transaction and repository adapters')
 s=s.replace('Native Vitest and Prisma are unavailable;','The native Vitest/Prisma stack was not run;')
 if f.name=='04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md':
  a=s.index('The fixture returns a DRAFT');z=s.index('\n\nDebug in order',a)
  s=s[:a]+'A DRAFT fixture with one policy reaches the write; the adapter verifies the transaction handle and records the requested target status. An ANALYST uses the actual policy and stops before lookup. Missing and invalid preconditions stop before transaction entry. Sentinel errors and primitive thrown values must retain identity unless the code is exactly P2025.'+s[z:]
 if f.name=='07-TRACE-LAB.md':s+='\nFor the success trace, record the exact object returned by the repository and require the service to return that same object. Also record the transaction handle passed to the update. These observations verify wiring; they do not make the mocked transaction an isolation test. Compare the actual permission and error modules with the adapters to see which behavior ran and which was simulated.\n'
 f.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
